le\": \"embedding Rich SVGs leaks styles\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"When embedding SVGs within a web page, the SVG styles \\\"leak\\\" in to the HTML. For instance the span style changes in the rest of the page. I'm not sure if there is some easy way to prevent that, but if not, perhaps we should generate a random ID for the SVG and update the styles to only use that UD.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 2584,\n      \"score\": 0.169,\n      \"title\": \"Link format string in docs to Python string formatting mini-language\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"In the code we see text_format: str = \\\"[progress.percentage]{task.percentage:>3.0f}%\\\", I would like this to be better documented or an hyperlink to where I could learn how to use that :>3.0f, I am looking for example to ensure the TextColumn text is always a fixed number of char, like 40, with an ellipsis, if it exceed, I was going to do it in Python before passing it to add_task, but I would like that pass the whole string to add_task instead and have it adjust the text output based on the \\\"progress\\\" TextColumn format.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 275,\n      \"score\": 0.161,\n      \"title\": \"[REQUEST] console print to string\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"I would like to use rich in a `__repr__` method, meaning that I have to get hold of a `str`. ```python console.print(table) ``` already prints the right thing for me; can I get that same output as a string?\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SPfEmiyWayCdv2Zdjj4inf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
